nd wander let your  mind drift and here there's absolutely  no structure or attempt to control you  just let it go where it goes and this  has been shown to have some very close  similarities to dreaming  so there is a lot of support for this  idea but on the whole we somewhat  demonized the whole concept of mind  wandering we're so focused on being in  the now and not living in the past or  not dreaming about the future that we  tell people to get out of their heads  and we act as though ever not being  mindful is a bad thing however great  breakthroughs come when you let your  mind wander and there's actually lots of  evidence now to support the health  benefits of doing just that all i'm  doing that's slightly different is i  tend to pick myself a big question  something that's inherently abstract and  huge and then ruminate on that i often  come back to the same questions things  that i find interesting and just  practice my problem-solving skills  i say there is now actually evidence  that mind-wandering and deep thought are  really healthy and good for your brain  the default mode network is the  specific pattern of brain areas that  activate when you're deep in thought  it's also called the task negative  network it's basically when you're not  putting your brain towards some kind of  complex task but just letting it wonder  mind wandering activates the default  mode network it's mainly what it's for  but at the same time we now know that  activation in the default mode network  correlates with not only creativity and  creative problem solving but also with  fluid intelligence so unsurprisingly  people who are better at thinking deeply  have more connectivity and activation in  this area are better at coming up with  creative solutions to problems now this  is a coveration not causation but we can  probably assume that if you spend time  practicing using your default mode  network you're going to get better at  using it in the same study it was also  shown th